# loop — environment template
#
# THE GRAND RULE: this file sets loop's baseline configuration, but any
# pipeline, room, or command can override any piece of it — or run fully
# self-contained. Per-field precedence everywhere:
#
#   explicit YAML/flag value  >  environment (shell > this file)  >  built-in default
#
# Overrides are partial: name just a model and inherit the family,
# endpoint, and key; name just a family and inherit the model.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you use:
#
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# How loop treats .env (internal/dotenv):
#   · ./.env is loaded on every command; the file named by LOOP_ENV_FILE
#     is loaded after it.
#   · Your real shell environment always wins — files only fill gaps.
#     Between the two files, ./.env wins over $LOOP_ENV_FILE.
#   · One KEY=VALUE per line. An "export " prefix, single/double quotes,
#     and trailing "  # comments" are all handled; malformed lines warn
#     with file:line and are skipped.
#   · .env is gitignored — keep real keys here, never in pipeline/room
#     YAML (those get committed and shared).

# ── Provider API keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of these is required for any pipeline stage or room persona that
# uses the matching provider. Unused ones can stay empty.
#
# Configure just ONE family and it becomes loop's default everywhere:
# commands, pipelines, and rooms with no (or partial) model blocks all
# follow the env. With both configured, anthropic stays the default;
# explicit YAML values always win when present.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Provider overrides (all optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Point a provider style at a different endpoint and/or model. With these
# set, YAML only needs `provider:` — no model id or base_url required.
# Resolution order everywhere: YAML value → env var → built-in default
# (official endpoint; claude-sonnet-4-5 / gpt-5).

# Your stated family. Only needed when BOTH families are configured
# (otherwise the single configured one is picked automatically);
# explicit `provider:` in YAML still wins over this.
# PROVIDER=

# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=          # e.g. a gateway or proxy speaking Anthropic's API
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=             # e.g. http://localhost:11434/v1 for Ollama
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=             # e.g. claude-sonnet-4-5
# OPENAI_MODEL=                # e.g. gpt-5, or llama3.3 for Ollama

# Custom key names via base_url (provider: openai + base_url at Groq etc.):
# set `api_key_env: GROQ_API_KEY` in the YAML, then define it here — any
# name works. Local endpoints that need no auth don't need a key at all.
#
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── loop knobs (all optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Extra env file loaded after ./.env. Handy for a shared team file or a
# per-project override chain. Paths are used as-is (no ~ expansion).
#
# LOOP_ENV_FILE=

# Node binary the cline executor should run (default: "node" on PATH).
# The SDK needs Node >= 22 — point this at a newer binary if your system
# node is older, e.g.:
#
# LOOP_NODE=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin/node

# Override where the cline host script lives. Default resolution order:
#   1. this variable
#   2. ~/.loop/executors/cline/index.mjs   (what `loop executor install cline` writes)
#   3. ./host/loop-cline-host/index.mjs    (repo-local dev checkout)
#
# LOOP_CLINE_HOST=
